.SH NAME
ktm-fs \- Reading and writing files, directories, file status and path names.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
import fs;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Reading and writing files, directories, file status and path names.
.SH TYPES
.SS FileStat
.EX
struct FileStat {
    u64 st_dev;
    u64 st_ino;
    u64 st_nlink;
    u32 st_mode;
    u32 st_uid;
    u32 st_gid;
    u64 st_rdev;
    i64 st_size;
    i64 st_blksize;
    i64 st_blocks;
    libc.timespec st_atim;
    libc.timespec st_mtim;
    libc.timespec st_ctim;
    libc.timespec st_btim;
};
.EE
.PP
Portable (across MacOS and Linux) stat structure
.SS FileKind
.EX
enum FileKind { file, dir, link, other };
.EE
.PP
What a FileStat describes: FileStat.kind()
.SS DirEntry
.EX
struct DirEntry {
    u8[] name;
    FileKind kind;
    String path;
};
.EE
.PP
One entry of a directory. \fBkind\fR is what the entry itself is: a symlink is a link, never what it points to. \fBname\fR and \fBpath\fR (the directory's path, a \fB/\fR, the name) are the Dir's own: they are valid until its next next() or close().
.SS Dir
.EX
struct Dir {
    libc.DIR *handle;
    String base;
    DirEntry entry;
};
.EE
.PP
An open directory: fs.openDir(path), next() until it gives null, then close() (\fBdefer d.close();\fR, or declare it \fBscoped\fR). "." and ".." are left out. Its fields are its own: use ok(), next() and close().
.SH CONSTANTS
.SS MAKE_DIR_DEFAULT
.EX
(libc.S_ISUID|libc.S_IRWXU|libc.S_IRWXG|libc.S_IROTH|libc.S_IXOTH)
.EE
.PP
Default fs.makeDir mode, 04775 (rwxrwxr-x; the set-user-ID bit means nothing on a directory), minus the umask: drwxr-xr-x with the usual 022.
.SS REMOVE_RECURSE
.EX
0x1
.EE
.SS REMOVE_FORCE
.EX
0x4
.EE
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS openDir
.EX
Dir openDir(u8[] path);
.EE
.PP
The directory at \fBpath\fR, open; ok() is false when it can't be opened (os.errno() says why), and next() then gives null
.SS list
.EX
vec.Vec<String> list(u8[] path, bool *ok = null);
.EE
.PP
The names in the directory at \fBpath\fR, sorted; *ok (when given) is false when it can't be read. Yours: free it with names.free().
.SS freeList
.EX
void freeList(vec.Vec<String> *names);
.EE
.PP
Frees what list() gave: the same as names.free(), which frees the names too
.SS walk
.EX
i32 walk(u8[] root, fn(DirEntry *, void *) bool visit, void *arg = null);
.EE
.PP
Every entry under the directory \fBroot\fR, at any depth: visit(entry, arg) for each, a directory before what is in it, without following symlinks (a link to a directory is visited, not entered). visit returns false to stop. 0 when every entry was visited, 1 when visit stopped it, -1 when a directory couldn't be read (os.errno() says why).
.SS join
.EX
String join(u8[] a, u8[] b);
String join(u8[] a, u8[] b, u8[] c);
.EE
.PP
\fBa/b\fR: one \fB/\fR between them; b alone when it is absolute or a is empty
.PP
\fBa/b/c\fR: join(join(a, b), c)
.SS exists
.EX
bool exists(u8[] path);
.EE
.PP
Is there something at \fBpath\fR (a symlink: is there something where it points)?
.SS makeDirAll
.EX
bool makeDirAll(u8[] path, i32 mode = MAKE_DIR_DEFAULT);
.EE
.PP
The directory \fBpath\fR made, with every missing parent, as makeDir(path, mode, true): true when \fBpath\fR is a directory afterwards (also when it already was), false with os.errno() set when not
.SS copyFile
.EX
bool copyFile(u8[] from, u8[] to);
.EE
.PP
The regular file \fBfrom\fR copied to \fBto\fR (made, or emptied first), with from's permission bits. true, or false with os.errno(): \fBfrom\fR isn't a regular file, the two are the same file, a read or a write failed (\fBto\fR is then removed).
.SS rename
.EX
bool rename(u8[] from, u8[] to);
.EE
.PP
\fBfrom\fR renamed to \fBto\fR (replacing a file there), on one filesystem: true, or false with os.errno() (EXDEV across filesystems: see move)
.SS move
.EX
bool move(u8[] from, u8[] to);
.EE
.PP
As rename(), and across filesystems a regular file is copied, then removed: true, or false with os.errno() (a directory can't move across filesystems)
.SS readAll
.EX
String readAll(u8[] path);
.EE
.PP
The whole file at path, a String that is yours (\fBdefer s.free();\fR), with a NUL after it; its ptr is null when the file can't be read (os.errno() says why). An empty file gives an empty String that has a ptr.
.SS writeAll
.EX
bool writeAll(u8[] path, u8[] data, i64 flags=libc.O_CREAT|libc.O_WRONLY|libc.O_TRUNC);
.EE
.PP
data into the file at path (made with 0644 when flags create it); false on an error
.SS currentDir
.EX
String currentDir();
.EE
.PP
The working directory, a String that is yours; its ptr is null on an error (getcwd's own block is libc malloc'd, which a String can't own)
.SS stat
.EX
i32 stat(FileStat *fst, u8[] path);
.EE
.PP
What is at path (fst filled; a symlink is followed to what it points to): 0, or -1 with errno set
.SS lstat
.EX
i32 lstat(FileStat *fst, u8[] path);
.EE
.PP
As stat, but a symlink is described itself (kind() is FileKind.link), not what it points to
.SS fstat
.EX
i32 fstat(FileStat *fst, i32 fd);
.EE
.PP
As stat, for the file open as fd
.SS realPath
.EX
String realPath(u8[] path);
.EE
.PP
The absolute path of path with every symlink, "." and ".." resolved (realpath(3)), a String that is yours; its ptr is null, with errno set, when a part of it doesn't exist or can't be read
.SS pread
.EX
i64 pread(i32 fd, u8[] buf, i64 off);
.EE
.PP
Up to buf.len bytes of fd from offset off into buf, without moving fd's offset (pread(2)): the bytes read, 0 at end of file, -1 with errno set
.SS pwrite
.EX
i64 pwrite(i32 fd, u8[] data, i64 off);
.EE
.PP
data written to fd at offset off, without moving fd's offset (pwrite(2)): the bytes written, or -1 with errno set
.SS changeDir
.EX
bool changeDir(u8[] path);
.EE
.PP
The working directory changed to path (\fB~\fR and \fB~/...\fR are under $HOME): true, or false with os.errno() set
.SS removeDir
.EX
bool removeDir(u8[] path, i64 flags=0);
.EE
.PP
The directory \fBpath\fR removed (with REMOVE_RECURSIVE, everything in it too): true, or false with os.errno() set
.SS remove
.EX
bool remove(u8[] path, i64 flags=0);
.EE
.PP
The file (or, with REMOVE_RECURSIVE, the directory) \fBpath\fR removed: true, or false with os.errno() set
.SS makeDir
.EX
bool makeDir(u8[] path, i32 mode=MAKE_DIR_DEFAULT, bool recurse=false);
.EE
.PP
The directory \fBpath\fR made (with recurse, every missing parent too): true when it is a directory afterwards (also when it already was), false with os.errno() set when not
.SS ext
.EX
u8[] ext(u8[] name);
.EE
.PP
The extension of a file name: from its first \fB\&.\fR that isn't followed by \fB/\fR or \fB\&.\fR to the end (".tar.gz" of "archive.tar.gz"), a view of it; empty when it has none
